# Canonical URL fix: /cladding-safety-scheme-under-11-metres.html and the clean
# extensionless URL were both resolving (200) and getting indexed separately by
# Google. The clean URL is canonical; force a 301 from the .html path to it.
# The "!" forces this redirect even though a static file exists at the .html path
# (Netlify skips _redirects for exact static-file matches unless forced).
/cladding-safety-scheme-under-11-metres.html   /cladding-safety-scheme-under-11-metres   301!

# Canonical URL fix: /index.html and / were both resolving (200) and getting
# indexed as near-duplicates by Google, and every internal link on the site
# pointed at /index.html rather than the root. Canonical tags, the sitemap and
# internal links now all point at /; force a 301 from /index.html to / so only
# one URL is ever served with 200.
/index.html   /   301!

# Canonical URL fix: avoid the literal /index.html path inside the Insights
# article/hub folders resolving as a separate 200 alongside the canonical
# trailing-slash directory URL used in the sitemap, internal links and
# canonical tags.
/insights/index.html   /insights/   301!
/insights/remediation-bill-2026-building-safety/index.html   /insights/remediation-bill-2026-building-safety/   301!
